{"step_index":1607,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:50:00Z","input_tokens":5478,"cache_read_tokens":116495,"output_tokens":2138,"thinking":"The `recomputeEverything()` function appears critical, as it triggers an invoice audit and UI update. This function calls `auditInvoice()`, `calculateTaxMetrics()`, and then `this.render()`, which suggests a complete re-evaluation of the invoice and a subsequent UI refresh. Focusing on how these functions interact is important to stopping the quantity being captured as tax.\n\n\nStrict tax extraction from the summary zone is essential, avoiding generic number matching. Observed that prior logic in the parser extracts tax values based on simple keyword matching and a broad numerical pattern, which caused incorrect GST capture.  Replacing the existing logic with the specified regular expressions for CGST, SGST, and IGST to ensure precise tax amount extraction.\n\n\nImplemented specific regular expressions for CGST, SGST, and IGST to accurately extract tax amounts. Added a check to avoid matching subtotal or total in words to prevent incorrect tax capture. Considered whether the second matched group, such as `cgstMatch[2]`, needs further handling.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport re\n\npat = re.compile(r\"(?:CGST|Central GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)\", re.I)\n\nlines = [\n    \"CGST @ 9%: ₹990.00\",\n    \"CGST 9%: 990.00\",\n    \"Central GST @ 9% : 990.00\",\n    \"CGST: 990.00\",\n    \"CGST: ₹1,980.00\",\n    \"CGST 9% 1,624.95\",\n    \"LED Tube Light 20W\",\n    \"Pack of 20\",\n    \"20W LED Batten\"\n]\n\nfor l in lines:\n    m = pat.search(l)\n    if m:\n        rate = m.group(1)\n        amt = m.group(2)\n        print(f\"MATCH: {l!r:30} -> rate={rate!r:6} amt={amt!r:10}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"NO MATCH: {l!r}\")\n'","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test line pattern regex"}}]}
