ng the 18% quick button requires retrieving the subtotal and determining the tax type (CGST/SGST or IGST) based on supplier and buyer GSTIN state codes. If the state codes match, CGST and SGST are calculated at half the tax rate, with IGST set to zero. If the codes differ, CGST and SGST are zeroed, and IGST is set to the full tax amount. The invoice header taxes need updating accordingly, followed by a re-audit. Now examining how this interacts with the audit engine.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"grep -rn -i \"buyer\" /Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Search for buyer in components"}}]}
